-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",72,{
[2273]="70009E37\n1\tYour allies may be found in Ost Guruth in the Lone-lands, Esteldín in the North Downs, and in places familiar to every people -- Combe for hobbits, the race of Men, and Beornings, and Gondamon for dwarf and Elf-kind. Golodir has asked you to return to three places where Sara Oakheart has been encountered in the past and speak with allies in those places.\t\n2\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar. You should return to Golodir and tell him the task is completed.\n",
[2274]="70009EBC\n1\tFind the Knight of Mordirith\tThe Knight of Mordirith can be found near an evil idol in the Chetwood, north-east of Combe. Constable Underhill told you how to find the threat in the Chetwood, which might be the knight you seek.\n2\tTalk to Constable Underhill\tConstable Underhill is outside The Comb and Wattle in Combe, south-west of the knight's camp. Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you return to Constable Underhill and let him know that the threat is ended.\n",
[2275]="70009EBF\n1\tFind the Knight of Mordirith\tThe Knight of Mordirith may be found near Ost Crithlanc, north-east of Esteldín. Daervunn told you of a new threat in the north, which may be the Knight you seek.\n2\tSpeak with Daervunn at Esteldin\tDaervunn is at Esteldín, south of the mouth of Ram Dúath. Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, You should return to Daervunn and let him know of your success.\n",
[2276]="70009EBD\n1\tFind the Knight of Mordirith\tThe Knight of Mordirith might be found north of Gondamon. Mathi Stouthand suggested that the threat to the north of Gondamon may be the Knight you seek.\n2\tTalk to Mathi\tMathi Stouthand is at Gondamon, south of the Knight's camp. Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you should return to Mathi Stouthand and let him know that you were successful.\n",
[2277]="70009EBE\n1\tFind the Knight of Mordirith\tThe Knight of Mordirith may be found somewhere within Harloeg, south and east of Ost Guruth. Frideric the Elder suggested that you might find the Knight of Mordirith in the southern bog.\n2\tTalk to Frideric the Elder\tFrideric the Elder is at Ost Guruth, north and west of Harloeg. Having defeated the Knight of Mordirith, you should return to Frideric the Elder and let him know of your success.\n",
[2278]="70048CF1\n1\tTalk to Frodo in the bower south-east of the field of Cormallen\tFrodo Baggins is in a bower on the south-eastern side of the field of Cormallen, recovering from his ordeal.\n2\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee in the bower\tSamwise Gamgee is in the bower in the south-east of the field of Cormallen.\n3\tTalk to Frodo Baggins in the bower\tFrodo Baggins is in the bower on the south-east of the field of Cormallen.\n4\tTalk to Peregrin Took in the bower\030Talk to Meriadoc Brandybuck in the bower\tPeregrin Took and Meriadoc Brandybuck are on the field of Cormallen.\n5\tTalk to Éomer on the field of Cormallen\030Talk to Prince Imrahil on the field of Cormallen\tÉomer of Rohan and Prince Imrahil of Dol Amroth are on the field of Cormallen.\n6\tTalk to Gimli on the field of Cormallen\030Talk to Legolas on the field of Cormallen\tLegolas and Gimli are on the field of Cormallen.\n7\tTalk to Radanir on the field of Cormallen\tRadanir and Aragorn are on the field of Cormallen.\n8\tTalk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen\tMithrandir is on the field of Cormallen.\n",
[2279]="700303CC\n1\tThere is a camp of Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn, north of Éomer's Vengeance. Horn wants you to go to the Orc camp beneath the Eaves of Fangorn and defeat the creatures there. You are also to keep your eyes open for your friends while you do.\t\n2\tThere is a camp of Orcs beneath the Eaves of Fangorn, north of Éomer's Vengeance. Horn wants you to go to the Orc camp beneath the Eaves of Fangorn and defeat the creatures there. You are also to keep your eyes open for your friends while you do.\t\n3\tTalk to the owner of the mysterious voice, south of the Orc camp\tYou heard a voice coming from a misty dell south of the Orc camp beneath the eaves of Fangorn, and should investigate.\n4\tTalk to Corudan at Éomer's Vengeance\tCorudan is at Éomer's Vengeance, south-east of the eaves of Fangorn. You encountered an Ent called Baldbark, and he sent you out of Fangorn with little ceremony.\n",
[2280]="70009EFD\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is on the other side of the cave at Gath Forthnír. Golodir instructed you to speak with Laerdan to learn how you can help him track down Amarthiel.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim. Laerdan instructed you to go to the Ranger-camp in Evendim to speak with the Ranger Calenglad.\n",
[2281]="70048CED\n1\tEnter his bower in the south-east of the field of Cormallen and find Frodo\tFrodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him in the south-east of the field of Cormallen.\n2\tTalk to Frodo inside the bower\tFrodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him on the field of Cormallen.\n3\tTalk to Frodo and experience 'Interlude: The Precious, At Last' or read the shortened account instead\tFrodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him on the field of Cormallen.\n4\tTalk to Frodo inside the bower\tFrodo is inside the bower that was prepared for him on the field of Cormallen.\n",
[2282]="700303CB\n1\tTalk to Horn in Eaworth\tHorn is already back at Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You have been reassured that your friends are safe, and now you should travel back to Eaworth with Horn and Corudan.\n2\tTalk to Éomer outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tÉomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Éomer said you were welcome to ride south with his men when he departed Eaworth.\n3\tTalk to Éomer and ride south to the Stone of Wyrgende\tÉomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. Éomer is ready to ride south when you are, but he has a number of destinations he wants to visit before turning for Edoras and home.\n4\tTalk to Éomer by the Stone of Wyrgende\tÉomer is standing by the Stone of Wyrgende. Éomer wishes to speak with you before departing for Snowbourn.\n",
[2283]="70009F3A\n1\tDiscover Amarthiel's plans at Annúminas\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim. Speak with Calenglad when you are ready to leave for Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger-camp at Tinnudir on the eastern shore of Lake Evendim. You should speak with Calenglad again, now that you have discovered Amarthiel's plans.\n",
[2284]="700303C9\n1\tMeet with Éomer in Snowbourn\tÉomer will meet you in Snowbourn outside the Mead Hall. You should ride south and speak again with Éomer in Snowbourn, in the Sutcrofts.\n",
[2285]="70048CEE\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir inside the bower that was provided for Frodo on the field of Cormallen\tMithrandir is in the bower that was prepared for Frodo on the field of Cormallen.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn on the field of Cormallen\tAragorn is on the field of Cormallen.\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen\tMithrandir is on the field of Cormallen.\n",
[2286]="700303CD\n1\tTalk to Grimstan in Snowbourn\tGrimstan is outside Reeve Fastred's home in Snowbourn, south-east of Éomer's location. Éomer has asked you to inquire of Grimstan why Reeve Fastred has not followed his command for his people to move across the Entwash for safety.\n2\tTalk to Éomer in Snowbourn\tÉomer is in Snowbourn, north-west of Fastred's house, outside the Mead Hall. You have heard Grimstan's explanation for Fastred's refusal to comply with Éomer's command, and should report it now to the Third Marshal.\n3\tCollect spears from Mordor corruptors in the Sutcrofts (total: 5)\030Collect fire-pots from Warg-riders in the Sutcrofts (total: 5)\tWarg-riders on the plains of the Sutcrofts wield fire-pots, and Mordor corruptors wield spears. Éomer has asked you to collect implements of destruction from Warg-riders and Mordor corruptors in the Sutcrofts. He wants to show them to the Reeve as evidence of what his people will face if they do not retreat across the Entwash.\n4\tBring Warg-rider and corruptor weapons to Éomer in Snowbourn\tÉomer is outside the Mead Hall in Snowbourn. You have collected implements of destruction from Warg-riders in the Sutcrofts, and should bring them to Éomer as he requested.\n",
[2287]="700303D2\n1\tTalk to and train with a Snowbourn villager\030Talk to and train with a member of the Snowbourn militia\030Talk to and train with a Snowbourn veteran\tVillagers, militia, and veterans can be found throughout Snowbourn. Éomer has asked you to train with villagers, militia, and veterans of Snowbourn, in order to prepare them in the event he cannot convince Fastred to move them across the Entwash.\n2\tTalk to Horn in Snowbourn\030Talk to Corudan in Snowbourn\tHorn and Corudan are in Snowbourn, by the fountain in the centre of town. You have trained with some of the people of Snowbourn, as have Horn and Corudan.\n3\tTalk to Éomer in Snowbourn\tÉomer is in Snowbourn, outside the Mead Hall. The Third Marshal of the Riddermark has returned from meeting with Reeve Fastred... and he does not look happy.\n",
[2288]="700303D4\n1\tTalk to Éomer in Snowbourn and ride to Edoras\tÉomer wants to ride to Edoras with you to consult with King Théoden about Fastred's refusal to move his people across the Entwash.\n2\tTalk to Horn by the Entwade\tHorn is at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts. The unthinkable has happened: Éomer has been imprisoned at the command of the King and you have been ordered never to cross the Entwash under pain of death.\n",
[2289]="700303D3\n1\tTalk to Hunbald at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts\tHunbald stands at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts. King Théoden has ordered you not to cross the Entwash under pain of death.\n2\tTalk to Corudan at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts\tCorudan is at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts.\n3\tTalk to Horn at the Entwade crossing, in the Sutcrofts\tHorn is at the Entwade crossing. Corudan has told you why he has hope for what tomorrow may bring, and has asked that you share his thoughts with Horn.\n",
[2290]="7000D9D3\n1\tTalk to Gandalf in Rivendell\tGandalf is in Bilbo's room on the first floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Aragorn has sent you to speak with Gandalf.\n",
[2291]="7001B780\n1\tTalk to Braiglinn at Imlad Lalaith\tBraiglinn is at Imlad Lalaith, on the shores of the Anduin, in Lothlórien. You have been told to speak with Braiglinn about the crossing of the Golden Host into Mirkwood.\n2\tBoard Calengoth's boat and assist Fuirgam with his tasks among the Mirk-eaves\tCalengoth is at the docks near Imlad Lalaith, on the shores of Anduin, in Lothlórien. Once you have made the crossing, you will find Fuirgam working to secure a foothold in Mirkwood. Calengoth, the launch officer, is waiting to see you to one of the boats that will carry you across Anduin with the first crossing. Once you have done so, seek out Fuirgam, the Elf in charge of securing a foothold for the Elves.\n3\tTalk to Alfirimbes at Echad Sirion\tAlfirimbes is waiting to speak with you in Echad Sirion. The Elves have established their foothold on the dark shores of Mirkwood and are ready to begin their push into the forest.\n",
[2292]="70021619\n1\tTalk to Arwen at Imdolen\tThe Lady Arwen is at Imdolen, on the slope that overlooks the road into the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell. Elrond has asked you to speak with his daughter Arwen before you depart with the Grey Company.\n2\tBring Aragorn's standard to Halbarad in Rivendell\tHalbarad is by the stables in Rivendell. Arwen has given you the standard she made for Aragorn and has asked you to bring it to Halbarad in Rivendell before the Grey Company departs.\n",
[2293]="700687B7\n1\tTalk to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib\tBashem has asked you to send books to Chakâr at Dâr Tabib. Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.\n2\tChakâr has asked you to give the books to listless patients in and around Dâr Tabib. Dâr Tabib is located in the south-west area of the Tor-gardens.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have delivered the last of the books to the patients of Dâr Tabib.\n",
[2294]="70026696\n1\tCollect flax plants (total: 4)\030Collect cherry-wood branches (total: 4)\030Collect twine (total: 4)\tThe supplies for Deluraw's boots can be found in Duillond and Celondim. Twine is at the docks of Celondim's harbour, branches can be found beneath the flowering trees of Duillond's fields, and flax plants can be picked along the road connecting the two Elven towns. You should collect Deluraw's ingredients and bring them to him to ensure a speedy delivery of Shrew-stomping boots.\n2\tBring the items to Deluraw\tDeluraw can be found in Duillond, near the cooking area. You should bring the boot-supplies to Deluraw, the boot-maker for the Festival.\n3\tTell Santmereth that the boot shipment is on schedule\tSantmereth can be found in the Festival Garden of Duillond. You should tell Santmereth that the boot shipment is in better shape now that you've lended a hand to the Boot-maker.\n",
[2295]="7004962F\n1\tTalk to Isnír\tYou should talk to Isnír.\n2\tTalk to Isnír\tIsnír can be found at the Udûn Foothold. You should speak with Isnír.\n",
[2296]="7005242D\n1\tTalk to Mílgamel at the Festival Grounds\tThree herbalists from Gondor are causing something of a stir at the Bree-land Festival Grounds, and Arn Bulrush has asked you to make sure they are happy... and quiet.\n2\tHelp Nethlas with 'A Natural Study'\tOne of Galathir's new apprentices, Nethlas, has been bothering people at the Festival Grounds with his master's research questions.\n3\tHelp Haerandel with 'The Blooms of Anarlossë'\tHaerandel has taken offence at something said by the herbalists from Gondor, and he wishes to correct it.\n4\tHelp Haerandel with 'To Depart in Springtime'\tHaerandel cannot believe that the Anarlossë might still thrive somewhere within the Shire, and he wants you to find his brother and tell him of the possibility before he sails into the West.\n5\tHelp Edlothon with 'The Promise of Sun-flowers'\tEdlothon does not know how the Anarlossë could have survived after so long, but he is willing to be convinced if you can find proof.\n6\tTalk to Arn Bulrush at the Festival Grounds\tArn Bulrush is at the Bree-land Festival Grounds.\n",
[2297]="70030416\n1\tDestroy Orc-barricades (total: 10)\030Collect wood-scraps from dismantled Orc-fortifications (total: 8)\tOrc-barricades can be found in the Orc-camps to the north and south-west of Walstow. Winsig wants you to destroy the Orc-barricades and collect wood-scraps from the wreckage.\n2\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig can be found in the Mead Hall of Walstow. You should return to Winsig with news of your success.\n",
[2298]="70059A0B\n1\tAid in the cleansing of the Red-maid\tThe Créoth will sacrifice themselves to the Red-maid to restore her strength and connexion to the corruption within the swamp. These Men deserve nothing better than death, and your presence in standing against the Red-maid may alert some part of her to the folly of her ways. You should let these Men die and strengthen the Red-maid, then defeat her. Perhaps a piece of her will understand that the corruption has grown too great, and she must return to the natural world of which she was once a part.\n",
[2299]="70059A71\n1\tDaily Reward -- Tier 2\tYou have returned to Garth Agarwen to defeat Naruhel, the Red-maid.\n",
[2300]="70059A72\n1\tDaily Reward -- Tier 3\tYou have returned to Garth Agarwen to defeat Naruhel, the Red-maid.\n",
[2301]="7005A464\n1\tDaily Reward -- Tier 1\tYou have returned to Garth Agarwen to defeat Naruhel, the Red-maid.\n",
[2302]="70051EF6\n1\tDefeat Storvâgûn\tYou have returned to the high cliffs above Helegrod to face Storvâgûn.\n",
[2303]="7004DE61\n1\tDefeat Thrâng\tDeep within the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu, Thrâng, the chieftain of the Ghâshfra, is ready to take on all comers who challenge his might.\n",
[2304]="7003FFED\n1\tDefeat spiders of Lhingroth (total: 10)\030Defeat Gúrnathron\tSpiders can be found to the east of Sardol and inside the cave of Lhingroth. You have discovered the spiders of Lhingroth, who pose a serious threat to the people of Sardol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have slain many spiders and defeated the brood-mother in Lhingroth.\n",
})
